    "result_text": "Green. Here's a summary of what I changed and why.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now **deterministic**: the first 12 hex characters of SHA\u2011256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`. Owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically, with no explicit linking. I kept each piece of logic in the unit that owns it rather than growing any class into a catch\u2011all:\n\n**`Households.java`** (the shared helper) \u2014 replaced the address\u2011keyed, `HH-`\u2011prefixed, opt\u2011in-only scheme with a single `householdId(lastName, postcode)` that returns the deterministic 12\u2011char hash (or `null` when there's no postcode, so postcode\u2011less owners have no household). Dropped the now\u2011unused `membersAt` / `resolveHouseholdId` / address key; kept `memberCount` (which is how household size keys off the household).\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 now simply stamps every built owner with the deterministic id (no repository, no back\u2011filling, no `sharesHousehold` branch), since the id is derivable from the owner's own fields.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** (the \"duplicate block\") \u2014 now rejects a create whose `(lastName, postcode)` household is already occupied (409), keyed directly off the computed `householdId`. `sharesHousehold=true` bypasses it, so a second owner in the household is created as a declared member.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 a declared member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is never flagged: it short\u2011circuits to `possibleDuplicate=false`. Its soft\u2011match logic is otherwise unchanged.\n\n**`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 unchanged in logic; it already sizes the household via `memberCount(householdId)`, which now uses the deterministic id.\n\nSupporting doc/consistency fixes: the exception now carries `householdId` (renamed from `identityKey`, message \"Household already registered: \u2026\"), the POST pipeline step comments, the `AddressNormalizer`/`IdentityKey`/`AssignHouseholdSize` Javadoc, and the OpenAPI `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` / `identityKey` descriptions.\n\n`IdentityKey` itself stays as the response\u2011surfaced value (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2014 it now naturally reflects the household via the deterministic id \u2014 but it's no longer what the duplicate block compares.\n\n## Behavior now matches the spec\n- Same lastName + postcode \u2192 same `householdId` automatically (even without `sharesHousehold`).\n- A second owner in that household \u2192 **409**, unless `sharesHousehold=true`.\n- With `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 created as a declared member and **not** flagged `possibleDuplicate`.\n- Duplicate detection and household size both key off the computed `householdId`.\n\nTest suite: the one acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) and the full build pass.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I made `householdId` **null when no postcode is present** (rather than hashing `lastName + '|' + \"\"`), so that postcode\u2011less owners aren't grouped into a household and don't trigger spurious 409s. Every test owner in the household test has a postcode, so this is consistent with the spec's `(lastName, postcode)` keying. If you'd prefer householdId to always be computed even without a postcode, that's a one\u2011line change in `Households.householdId`.",
